{"id":130741,"title":"Parallel sphere rendering","url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=parallel volume rendering","final_url":"https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/m2/1/high_res_d/390590.pdf","year":null,"kind":"link","source":"os:digital.library.unt.edu","doi":null,"arxiv":null,"sha256":"2461ec516f89fe18ea586bce1d53437601890f7037fc200b1d22779f39281711","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"url","fetched_at":1793305926.5960138,"text_chars":40338,"abstract":"Sphere rendering is an important method for visualizing molecular dynamics data. This paper presents a parallel algorithm that is almost 90 times faster than current graphics workstations. To render extremely large data sets and large images, the algorithm uses the MIMD features of the supercomputers to divide up the data, render independent partial images, and then finally composite the multiple partial images using an optimal method. The algorithm and performance results are presented for the CM-5 and the M.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/m2/1/high_res_d/390590.pdf","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=parallel volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=volume rendering library","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=bounding sphere volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=distributed shared virtual memory volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=3d table animation volume rendering","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=parallel direct compositing","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=parallel image compositing","https://digital.library.unt.edu/ark:/67531/metadc678482/?q=silhouette image volume rendering"],"cited_by":[{"path":"6889-sort-last-parallel-rendering.md","name":"Sort-last Parallel Rendering","k":6},{"path":"17204-parallel-sphere-rendering-with-global-z-buffer-reduction.md","name":"Parallel Sphere Rendering with Global Z-Buffer Reduction","k":1}]}